00:48:37.000 --> 00:49:23.000
She would flatter George and earn his sympathy by discussing her marital problems with him. A Mensa murder mystery weekend that George was hosting was Agent Gorak's inn, and she sent him a letter posing as Sherry asking to attend. Over the course of that weekend, Agent Gorak looked for clues and took numerous photographs. She took particular note of a pamphlet George had written up for the weekend, which was titled Voodoo for Fun and Profit. The title was a nod to the theme of the murder mystery, which centered about Voodoo practitioners. An excerpt of the pamphlet read,
她会奉承乔治，并通过与他讨论婚姻问题来赢得他的同情。乔治正在举办的一个门萨谋杀之谜周末活动是戈拉克探员的切入点，她以雪莉的名义写信给他，要求参加。在那个周末，戈拉克探员寻找线索并拍摄了大量照片。她特别注意到了乔治为周末活动写的一本小册子，标题是《巫毒：为了乐趣和利润》。标题是对谋杀之谜主题的致敬，该主题围绕巫毒教从业者展开。小册子的一段摘录写道：

75
00:49:23.000 --> 00:50:14.000
Few voodooists believe they can be killed by psychic means, but no one doubts that he can be poisoned. When a death threat appears on the doorstep, prudent people throw out all their food and watch what they eat. Hardly anyone dies from magic. Most items on the doorstep are just a neighbor's way of saying, I don't like you, move or else. To investigators, this appeared to be a not-so-subtle reference to the poisoned Coca-Cola bottles that appeared at the car home. Over the course of eight months, Agent Gorak built a friendship with George. She complained to him about her fictional ex-husband, hoping it might coax a confession out of him.
很少有巫毒教徒相信他们会被心理手段杀死，但没有人怀疑他们会被毒死。当死亡威胁出现在门口时，谨慎的人会扔掉所有的食物并注意饮食。几乎没有人死于魔法。门口的大多数物品只是邻居表达我不喜欢你，搬走否则后果自负的一种方式。对调查人员来说，这似乎是对出现在卡尔家门口的有毒可口可乐瓶的含蓄指涉。在八个月的时间里，戈拉克探员与乔治建立了友谊。她向他抱怨她虚构的前夫，希望这能诱使他坦白。

76
00:50:14.000 --> 00:51:09.000
The undercover operation was a long, slow process. Eventually, the higher-ups began complaining about the lack of results. Then, a breakthrough finally occurred when George and his wife moved to Sebring in November 1989. Agent Gorak would ask to rent their home in Al-Turus, giving her unfettered access to the property. Agent Gorak moved into George Treepower's home on Tuesday, December 12, 1989. That evening, crime scene technicians descended on the property. They rubbed cotton balls dipped in nitric acid along surfaces throughout the house, looking for traces of thallium. Sinks, drains and the inside of cabinets were all swabbed.
卧底行动是一个漫长而缓慢的过程。最终，上级开始抱怨缺乏成果。然后，当乔治和他的妻子于1989年11月搬到塞布林时，终于取得了突破。戈拉克探员要求租下他们在阿尔图拉斯的房子，这让她可以不受限制地进入该房产。戈拉克探员于1989年12月12日星期二搬进了乔治·特雷帕尔的家。那天晚上，犯罪现场技术人员涌入该房产。他们用蘸有硝酸的棉球擦拭整个房子的表面，寻找铊的痕迹。水槽、排水管和橱柜内部都被擦拭取样。

77
00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:51.000
The garage workshop was also searched. George hadn't bothered to clear it out when he moved. Empty spray paint cans, scraps of wood and garden supplies were littered everywhere. The floor was covered with sawdust, nails and broken glass. There were also jugs filled with various liquids. A couple of small bottles were found on George's workbench. One was made of brown glass and had a white residue inside. These were packaged up to be examined at an FBI lab.
车库车间也进行了搜查。乔治搬走时没有清理它。空喷漆罐、木头碎片和园艺用品到处都是。地板上覆盖着锯末、钉子和碎玻璃。还有装满各种液体的罐子。在乔治的工作台上发现了几个小瓶子。一个是棕色玻璃做的，里面有白色残留物。这些被打包送往联邦调查局实验室进行检查。

78
00:51:51.000 --> 00:52:47.000
While investigators were waiting for the results to come back, Agent Gorak met with George, as Sherry, to tell him that she knew about the poisoning next door. She hoped that he might be shocked into giving something away. Although George seemed rattled, he didn't say anything incriminating. In March 1990, one year after Peggy Carr's death, the results from the property search came back. The brown bottle found in the garage workshop had tested positive for thallium. At 8am on Saturday, April 7, 1990, Agent Gorak dialed George Trepal's home number in Sebring from a mobile phone. When George came to the phone, Agent Gorak said in a shaky voice,
当调查人员等待结果时，戈拉克探员以雪莉的身份与乔治会面，告诉他她知道隔壁中毒的事。她希望他能因为震惊而泄露一些东西。虽然乔治看起来很慌乱，但他没有说任何有罪的话。1990年3月，在佩吉·卡尔去世一年后，房产搜查结果出来了。在车库车间发现的棕色瓶子检测出铊呈阳性。1990年4月7日星期六上午8点，戈拉克探员用手机拨打了乔治·特雷帕尔在塞布林的家中电话。当乔治接电话时，戈拉克探员用颤抖的声音说：

79
00:52:47.000 --> 00:53:21.000
Hi George, it's Sherry. Those two investigators came to my house again this morning. They were asking about you again, something about chemicals. I don't know what they're talking about. Do you? George told Agent Gorak to calm down as she grew increasingly distraught. The two chatted for a while, then Agent Gorak heard a disturbance on George's end. In a calm tone, George suddenly said,
嗨，乔治，我是雪莉。那两名调查员今天早上又来我家了。他们又在问关于你的事，说是关于化学品的。我不知道他们在说什么。你知道吗？当戈拉克探员变得越来越心烦意乱时，乔治让她冷静下来。两人聊了一会儿，然后戈拉克探员听到乔治那边有动静。乔治突然平静地说：

80
00:53:21.000 --> 00:54:16.000
Sherry, by coincidence, the police are here. You'll have to call back Monday. While Agent Gorak had been talking to George, investigators had been making their way to his home, armed with a warrant for his arrest. George's wife Diana tried to refuse their entry and had to be pulled from the doorway to the front yard. Diana yelled and swore at the police, but George seemed relaxed as he met them at the top of the stairs, wearing only a pair of women's bikini briefs. He got dressed and was then placed under arrest for the murder of Peggy Carr. Meanwhile, investigators carried out a search of George's sea-bring residence. Amongst his belongings, they found a loose-leaf binder filled with pages taken from scientific textbooks.
雪莉，巧合的是，警察来了。你得周一再打来。当戈拉克探员与乔治通话时，调查人员带着逮捕令前往他的家。乔治的妻子戴安娜试图拒绝他们进入，不得不被从门口拉到前院。戴安娜对警察大喊大叫并咒骂，但乔治在楼梯顶端迎接他们时显得很放松，只穿了一条女式比基尼内裤。他穿好衣服，随后因谋杀佩吉·卡尔而被捕。与此同时，调查人员搜查了乔治在塞布林的住所。在他的财物中，他们发现了一个活页夹，里面装满了从科学教科书中撕下的页面。

81
00:54:16.000 --> 00:55:04.000
George had written a title on the front. General Poisoning Guides Inside, the binder featured information for law enforcement on identifying poisoning cases. Another book titled Poison Detection in Human Organs had a detailed paragraph on thallium. A large amount of bondage equipment and toys were found in a closet. In another room, a secret compartment behind a pegboard lined with tools revealed a tiny, sound-proofed room. It had black-panelled walls and no windows. On the floor was a wooden platform the size of a bed with manacles attached.
乔治在封面上写了一个标题：通用中毒指南。在活页夹内，收录了供执法部门识别中毒案件的信息。另一本名为《人体器官中的毒物检测》的书详细介绍了铊。在一个壁橱里发现了大量的束缚设备和玩具。在另一个房间里，一个衬有工具的钉板后面的秘密隔间里露出了一个微小的隔音室。它有黑色镶板墙，没有窗户。地板上是一个床大小的木制平台，上面系着手铐。

82
00:55:04.000 --> 00:56:03.000
It looked as though the room had only recently been built and testing revealed nothing untoward, such as blood or other bodily fluids. But it looked to detectives as though George had been making a torture chamber with the space to tie someone up. News of George Tree Powell's arrest came as a shock to his fellow Mensa members. They told the media they couldn't believe that such a great guy would be capable of murder. To them, George was a friendly man who rescued stray cats. Peggy Carr's children were also in disbelief that their eccentric former neighbour could do such a thing, especially over something as minor as loud music. George Tree Powell pleaded not guilty and his trial began in January 1991.
看起来这个房间是最近才建成的，测试显示没有异常情况，比如血液或其他体液。但对侦探们来说，看起来乔治一直在利用这个空间建造一个折磨室，用来把人绑起来。乔治·特雷帕尔被捕的消息让他的门萨成员感到震惊。他们告诉媒体，他们无法相信这样一个好人会做出谋杀这种事。对他们来说，乔治是一个救助流浪猫的友好男人。佩吉·卡尔的孩子们也不敢相信他们古怪的前邻居会做出这种事，尤其还是因为音乐声大这种小事。乔治·特雷帕尔拒不认罪，他的审判于1991年1月开始。

83
00:56:03.000 --> 00:57:07.000
FBI scientists testified about the way Peggy had been poisoned and the bottles with traces of thallium found in George's home. Agent Susan Gorak was the state's star witness. The day after she testified about her undercover work on the case, George's wife Diana approached the agent outside the courtroom and screamed, I hope you know just what a bitch you are. George Tree Powell's defence team argued that the evidence against their client was entirely circumstantial. They pointed to other possible suspects whom they felt investigators hadn't considered, such as George's wife Diana. They also queried why detectives had been so quick to rule out Peggy Carr's husband, given that the couple had been having marital problems. They cited a Jack Daniels bottle that was found in the Carr's shed and was filled with some sort of pesticide.
联邦调查局的科学家作证说佩吉是如何中毒的，以及在乔治家中发现的带有铊痕迹的瓶子。苏珊·戈拉克探员是州政府的明星证人。在她就此案的卧底工作作证后的第二天，乔治的妻子戴安娜在法庭外接近该探员并尖叫道：我希望你知道你是个多么贱的女人。乔治·特雷帕尔的辩护团队辩称，针对他们客户的证据完全是间接的。他们指出了调查人员认为没有考虑到的其他潜在嫌疑人，例如乔治的妻子戴安娜。他们还质疑为什么侦探们如此迅速地排除了佩吉·卡尔的丈夫，因为这对夫妇一直有婚姻问题。他们引用了在卡尔家棚子里发现的一个杰克丹尼酒瓶，里面装满了某种杀虫剂。

84
00:57:07.000 --> 00:58:06.000
Health officials had never tested the pesticide, so couldn't say whether or not it had thallium in it. A search of the Carr's garage apartment had also revealed a trace of thallium beneath the sink. However, the state pointed out that this trace had been so minuscule that a second test of the sink found no thallium at all. It was possible the first test had been a false reading. The trial ran for four weeks. The jury ultimately found George Tree Powell guilty of 15 charges, including one count of first-degree murder and six counts of attempted first-degree murder. At the jury's recommendation, George was sentenced to death by lethal injection. 32 years later, George Tree Powell remains on death row.
卫生官员从未检测过这种杀虫剂，因此无法确定其中是否含有铊。对卡尔家车库公寓的搜查也在水槽下发现了铊的痕迹。然而，州政府指出，这种痕迹非常微小，以至于对水槽的第二次测试根本没有发现铊。第一次测试可能是读数错误。审判持续了四个星期。陪审团最终裁定乔治·特雷帕尔犯有15项罪名，包括一项一级谋杀罪和六项一级谋杀未遂罪。根据陪审团的建议，乔治被判处注射死刑。32年后，乔治·特雷帕尔仍被关在死囚牢房里。

85
00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:56.000
He is now 74 years old and maintains his innocence. All of his appeals have been unsuccessful. To this day, some people believe that George Tree Powell is innocent. His supporters point to the circumstantial nature of the case against him and maintain that detectives had tunnel vision from the start. They describe George as a gentle man they've never known to be violent. But investigators, including Agent Susan Gorak, who spent a year getting to know George Tree Powell, have no doubt that the man dubbed the Mensa murderer is guilty. In 1995, Agent Gorak co-wrote a book about the case with the journalist Geoffrey Goode.
他现在74岁，坚称自己无罪。他所有的上诉都失败了。直到今天，有些人仍然认为乔治·特雷帕尔是无辜的。他的支持者指出了针对他的案件的间接性质，并坚持认为侦探们从一开始就有思维定势。他们形容乔治是一个他们从未听说过有暴力倾向的温和男人。但包括花了一年时间了解乔治·特雷帕尔的苏珊·戈拉克探员在内的调查人员毫不怀疑，这个被称为门萨杀手的人是有罪的。1995年，戈拉克探员与记者杰弗里·古德合著了一本关于此案的书。

86
00:58:56.000 --> 00:59:39.000
Titled Poison Mind, the book details Agent Gorak's undercover work as Sherry Gwynn and examines the impact that the case had on Peggy Carr's family. Peggy's children drifted away from their stepfather Pie Carr and his kids. They all have mixed feelings about George Tree Powell's death sentence. Pie Carr told the Ledger newspaper that he's still waiting for the day when he can see the death sentence carried out. Quote, I still want to be there when he's executed, but I don't have anything to say to him. I don't think I could control myself if I was to talk to him.
书名为《毒心》，详细介绍了戈拉克探员作为雪莉·格温的卧底工作，并审视了此案对佩吉·卡尔家庭的影响。佩吉的孩子们逐渐疏远了他们的继父派伊·卡尔和他的孩子们。他们对乔治·特雷帕尔的死刑判决有着复杂的情绪。派伊·卡尔告诉《分类账》报纸，他仍在等待死刑执行的那一天。引用原文，我仍然想在他被处决时在场，但我没什么话要对他说。如果我和他说话，我想我无法控制自己。

87
00:59:39.000 --> 01:00:31.000
Two of Peggy's children, Dwayne and Jelena, say they have forgiven George Tree Powell and don't believe he should be executed. But Peggy's son, Alan, disagrees. He believes that George losing his life is the consequence he must suffer for his actions. Alan, Jelena and Dwayne have all found their own ways to keep their mother's memory alive. Dwayne had to battle with physical trauma as well as emotional pain. The poisoning that took his mother's life also led to Dwayne losing half his body weight and spending three months in hospital. He had to use a wheelchair until he could walk again. Although he eventually made a full recovery, he struggled in the aftermath.
佩吉的两个孩子，德韦恩和杰琳娜，说他们已经原谅了乔治·特雷帕尔，不认为他应该被处决。但佩吉的儿子艾伦不同意。他认为乔治失去生命是他必须为自己的行为付出的代价。艾伦、杰琳娜和德韦恩都找到了各自的方式来铭记他们的母亲。德韦恩不仅要面对情感上的痛苦，还要与身体上的创伤作斗争。夺走他母亲生命的毒药也导致德韦恩体重减半，并在医院住了三个月。他不得不使用轮椅，直到能再次行走。虽然他最终完全康复，但在那之后他过得很艰难。

88
01:00:31.000 --> 01:00:36.000
While going through some difficulties, he found strength in writing a letter to Peggy. Today, he wishes his mother was still alive so she could meet his wife and see how he's turned his life around. Alan thinks of Peggy anytime he sees a waitress whose apron pockets jingle with the sound of coins. Whenever Jelena wants to connect with her mother, she says aloud, Mama, I love you. There aren't comments yet for this episode. Click on any sentence in the transcript to leave a comment.
在经历了一些困难时，他从给佩吉写信中找到了力量。今天，他希望母亲还活着，这样她就能见到他的妻子，看到他如何改变了自己的生活。每当艾伦看到围裙口袋里发出硬币叮当声的女服务员时，他就会想起佩吉。每当杰琳娜想与母亲联系时，她都会大声说，妈妈，我爱你。这一集还没有评论。点击转录中的任何句子即可发表评论。
